{
  "gang": "cactus",
  "displayName": "Cactus",
  "aliases": [
    "CACTUS"
  ],
  "status": "active",
  "activeSince": "2023",
  "lineage": "Reported overlap with ex-Black Basta operators (shared BackConnect / Teams vishing playbook, 2025)",
  "summary": "Cactus emerged in March 2023 targeting large enterprises via edge-device exploitation (Fortinet VPN, Qlik Sense CVE-2023-41265/41266/48365, Ivanti Sentry CVE-2023-38035). In 2025 it adopted the Black Basta playbook of email bombing plus Microsoft Teams vishing to get victims to start Quick Assist, followed by OneDriveStandaloneUpdater DLL side-loading of the QakBot-linked BackConnect malware. Post-exploitation uses RMM (AnyDesk, ManageEngine UEMS, Splashtop), SSH/Plink tunnels, WinRM, Rclone, ESXi SSH/firewall tampering and a self-encrypting payload.",
  "uniqueTraits": [
    "Encryptor is itself AES-encrypted and only unpacked with a key supplied at run time (-i/-r flags, 7-Zip/batch unpacking)",
    "Qlik Sense Scheduler exploitation (CVE-2023-41265/41266/48365) pulling ManageEngine UEMS disguised as Qlik files",
    "2025: email bombing + Teams vishing -> Quick Assist -> .bpx/.cab payload -> OneDriveStandaloneUpdater.exe side-loading wscapi.dll (BackConnect)",
    "BackConnect C2 list in HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\TitanPlus",
    "ESXi: enable root SSH, disable execInstalledOnly and firewall, run socks.out (SystemBC)"
  ],
  "insufficientReporting": false,
